<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador sells $40 million in zero coupon bonds.</title>
<headline>Ecuador sells $40 million in zero coupon bonds.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador said Thursday it sold $40 million in 357-day zero-coupon bonds in an auction held simultaneously on the Quito and Guayaquil stock exchanges.</p>
<p>The bonds were sold at an average discount price of 91.98 and an average yield of 8.58 percent.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said it received bids for a total of $229.16 million.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429))</p>
